<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 40,500 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 46.316 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 21,500 tonnes, in the U.K. 6,000, in Denmark 6,000, in Belgium 6,000, in Germany 500 and in Spain 500 tonnes, it added.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
